===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|riddil}}, {{m|enm|ridelle||sieve}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|hriddel||sieve}}, alteration of earlier {{m|ang|hridder}}, {{m|ang|hrīder}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*hrīdrą||sieve}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*hrid-||to shake}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*krey-}}. Akin to {{cog|de|Reiter||sieve}}, {{cog|non|hreinn||pure, clean}}, {{cog|goh|hreini||pure, clean}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐍂𐌰𐌹𐌽𐍃||clean, pure}}. More at {{l|en|rinse}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|sieve}} A [[sieve]] with coarse [[mesh]]es, usually of wire, for separating coarser materials from finer, as chaff from grain, cinders from ashes, or gravel from sand.
# A [[board]] with a row of [[pin]]s, set [[zigzag]], between which wire is drawn to [[straighten]] it.

